		<key>instructionSections</key>
		<array>
			<dict>
				<key>id</key><string>D1111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111</string><key>title</key><string>Noodles</string><key>steps</key>
				<array>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001</string><key>text</key><string>Fill the 8-quart pot with cold, fresh water to 1 inch below the top.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000002</string><key>text</key><string>Salt the water with a heaping tablespoon of salt and bring it to a rolling boil.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000003</string><key>text</key><string>Add the noodles and cook according to the package directions for firm or al dente, usually about 6 minutes.</string><key>duration</key><dict><key>seconds</key><integer>360</integer></dict></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000004-0000-4000-8000-000000000004</string><key>text</key><string>Strain the noodles immediately and transfer them to the baking dish.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000005-0000-4000-8000-000000000005</string><key>text</key><string>Toss the noodles with a bit of olive oil, 2 tablespoons butter, black pepper, Italian seasoning, garlic powder, and onion powder to taste.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000006-0000-4000-8000-000000000006</string><key>text</key><string>Set the noodles aside while preparing the sauce.</string></dict>
				</array>
			</dict>
			<dict>
				<key>id</key><string>D2222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222</string><key>title</key><string>Sauce and assembly</string><key>steps</key>
				<array>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000007-0000-4000-8000-000000000007</string><key>text</key><string>Preheat the oven to 400°F.</string><key>temperature</key><dict><key>value</key><dict><key>numerator</key><integer>400</integer><key>denominator</key><integer>1</integer></dict><key>unit</key><string>fahrenheit</string></dict></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000008-0000-4000-8000-000000000008</string><key>text</key><string>Finely dice the onions. Sauté them in a generous amount of butter, about 2 tablespoons, seasoning with Montreal steak seasoning, salt, and pepper to taste.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000009-0000-4000-8000-000000000009</string><key>text</key><string>Cook until softened or very lightly browned. There is no need for much caramelization here; the peas will provide ample sweetness.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E000000A-0000-4000-8000-00000000000A</string><key>text</key><string>Add the cream of mushroom soup, milk, and tuna. Warm through, then add a dash of Worcestershire sauce and cayenne pepper to taste.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E000000B-0000-4000-8000-00000000000B</string><key>text</key><string>Taste the sauce. At this point it should be a bit “too much”: just a bit too salty, too savory, and tuna-forward. It should otherwise be well balanced and look a bit runny. This is ideal; the noodles will absorb and soften the sauce.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E000000C-0000-4000-8000-00000000000C</string><key>text</key><string>Cook just until simmering. CAUTION: It is very easy to burn this sauce! A very gentle fond is nice, but the difference between “fond” and “burned electrical wire” taste is about 15 seconds of high heat, so tame that heat or pay attention.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E000000D-0000-4000-8000-00000000000D</string><key>text</key><string>Immediately pour the sauce over the noodles. Add the frozen peas and fold everything together gently.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E000000E-0000-4000-8000-00000000000E</string><key>text</key><string>Place the baking dish in the center of the preheated oven, preferably on a rimmed sheet tray to catch possible drips. Check after 10 minutes; the hotdish should just begin to bubble.</string><key>duration</key><dict><key>seconds</key><integer>600</integer></dict><key>temperature</key><dict><key>value</key><dict><key>numerator</key><integer>400</integer><key>denominator</key><integer>1</integer></dict><key>unit</key><string>fahrenheit</string></dict></dict>
				</array>
			</dict>
			<dict>
				<key>id</key><string>D3333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333</string><key>title</key><string>Topping</string><key>steps</key>
				<array>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E000000F-0000-4000-8000-00000000000F</string><key>text</key><string>While the hotdish begins baking, crush the croutons and Ritz crackers into a coarse powder.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000010-0000-4000-8000-000000000010</string><key>text</key><string>Melt 2 tablespoons butter and stir it into the topping.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000011-0000-4000-8000-000000000011</string><key>text</key><string>Season with pepper. Salt will not be needed.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000012-0000-4000-8000-000000000012</string><key>text</key><string>Optionally—but highly recommended—grate pecorino into the topping and stir to combine.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000013-0000-4000-8000-000000000013</string><key>text</key><string>Once the hotdish has begun to bubble, top it evenly and return it to the oven to brown.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000014-0000-4000-8000-000000000014</string><key>text</key><string>Check after 8 minutes, then every 2 minutes thereafter.</string><key>duration</key><dict><key>seconds</key><integer>480</integer></dict></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000015-0000-4000-8000-000000000015</string><key>text</key><string>Brown to the desired level and remove promptly.</string></dict>
					<dict><key>id</key><string>E0000016-0000-4000-8000-000000000016</string><key>text</key><string>Let the hotdish rest for about 10 minutes before serving.</string><key>duration</key><dict><key>seconds</key><integer>600</integer></dict></dict>
				</array>
			</dict>
		</array>
	</dict>
